{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "19", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "22", "S": "33"}}, "news": [{"title": "Pay house tax in three instalments, Prayagraj civic body offers full interest waiver", "para": "Prayagraj Municipal Corporation has launched a one-time settlement scheme for house tax dues. This initiative offers a complete waiver on accumulated interest for property owners. Eligible individuals can pay their principal house tax in up to three installments. The scheme aims to encourage settlement of long-pending property tax liabilities. Property owners can apply through zonal offices or the municipal corporation website.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/pay-house-tax-in-three-instalments-prayagraj-civic-body-offers-full-interest-waiver/133337251?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-165102/133337251.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Four buildings in Gurugram DLF phase-III sealed for 'unauthorised construction'", "para": "Four buildings were sealed in Gurugram for unauthorized construction and commercial activities.  Unused stilt areas were demolished, and illegal PGs and guest houses were sealed.  Approximately 1.5 kilometers of the Right of Way was cleared of encroachments.  The enforcement wing of the Town and Country Planning Department led the drive.  District Town Planner Amit Madholiya oversaw the operations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/four-buildings-in-gurugram-dlf-phase-iii-sealed-for-unauthorised-construction/133336972?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-329664/133336972.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Gujarat: Housing loan ticket size up 72%, takers decline 28% in Q1 FY27", "para": "In Gujarat, a trend is emerging in the housing market where fewer buyers are opting for home loans. Those who do are securing larger amounts, a reflection of the soaring property and construction costs in the region. Meanwhile, affluent buyers are still acquiring bigger homes, while the mass market grapples with rising prices that have made affordability a significant challenge.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/housing-finance/gujarat-housing-loan-ticket-size-up-72-takers-decline-28-in-q1-fy27/133336713?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-536880/133336713.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "housing-finance"}]}